From: linux-omarchy-aarch64
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: skip clock stop on the Vivobook S15
 S5507QA

On the ASUS Vivobook S 15 S5507QA (X1P-42-100, asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4)
the WSA SoundWire controller, 6b10000.soundwire, holds the two WSA884x
amplifiers. After it exits clock stop on runtime resume those amplifiers
report every register as 0x21, and wsa884x keeps the PA off. The DAPM
path is fully on and the PCM is RUNNING, but nothing comes out of the
speakers. This is the same failure patch 2438 works around on Glymur's
v3.1.0 controllers, which this X1P controller is not.

Keeping every qcom-soundwire controller out of runtime suspend
(power/control=on) makes the speakers play, confirmed on this machine.
Mark clock stop unsupported when the machine compatible is
asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4, the board compatible in
x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s15.dts, so runtime suspend skips the clock stop
and runtime resume resets the controller and re-enumerates, as v3.1.0
already does. Other machines keep the 2438 behaviour.

---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -667,10 +667,15 @@
 		/*
 		 * Peripherals on v3.1.0 controllers (Glymur) often come back
 		 * from a clock stop unattached, or attached but returning
-		 * garbage for every register read. Reset the controller and
-		 * re-enumerate on runtime resume instead, as at probe.
+		 * garbage for every register read. The Vivobook S 15 S5507QA
+		 * (asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4) does the same on its WSA bus: the
+		 * WSA884x amplifiers answer every register with 0x21 and the
+		 * PA stays off. Reset and re-enumerate instead of exiting
+		 * clock stop.
 		 */
-		ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported = ctrl->version >= SWRM_VERSION_3_1_0;
+		ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported =
+			ctrl->version >= SWRM_VERSION_3_1_0 ||
+			of_machine_is_compatible("asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4");
 		/* Now compare with entries */
 		list_for_each_entry_safe(slave, _s, &bus->slaves, node) {
 			if (sdw_compare_devid(slave, id) == 0) {
